/**
 * The `word-break` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets whether
 * line breaks appear wherever the text would otherwise overflow its content box.
 *
 * Initial: normal. Inherited: yes.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - auto-phrase: Has the same effect as `word-break: normal` except that language-specific analysis
 * is performed to improve word breaks by not placing them in the middle of natural phrases.
 * - break-all: To prevent overflow, word breaks should be inserted between any two characters
 * (excluding Chinese/Japanese/Korean text).
 * - break-word: Has the same effect as `overflow-wrap: anywhere` combined with `word-break:
